# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# iam-tender-acl — local dev environment
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy to .env and adjust. `make setup` copies this file if .env is absent.
# `make run` sources .env automatically if it exists.
#
# These defaults match docker-compose.yml (`make compose-up`): Postgres on
# host port 5536 (container 5432), Valkey on host port 6382 (container
# 6379) — offset from the standard ports so both can run side by side with
# sibling repos' own docker-compose stacks on the same machine. The binary
# self-migrates at startup (see cmd/tender-acl/migrate.go) using
# MIGRATION_DATABASE_URL — there is no separate migrate service/Job to wait
# on.

# ── Application ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
APP_NAME=iam-tender-acl
APP_ENV=dev
# 8080 is org-membership-service's own port (APP_PORT, non-configurable
# there) — running both natively side by side needs a distinct port here.
HTTP_PORT=8086
METRICS_PORT=9090
LOG_LEVEL=debug
ENVIRONMENT=development

# ── PostgreSQL ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DATABASE_URL is the RUNTIME app role (tender_acl_app) — it has no
# BYPASSRLS, so Row-Level Security is enforced. Never point this at the
# migration/superuser role.
DATABASE_URL=postgres://tender_acl_app:tender_acl_app_dev_password@localhost:5536/tender_acl?sslmode=disable

# MIGRATION_DATABASE_URL is the BYPASSRLS role the binary itself uses ONLY
# for the startup migration run (cmd/tender-acl/migrate.go, LLD §7.4).
# Falls back to DATABASE_URL if unset, which will fail here since
# tender_acl_app cannot apply schema migrations — set this explicitly. In
# docker-compose that's simply the postgres superuser; production points
# it at a dedicated tender_acl_migrator role. `make migrate-up`/
# `migrate-down`/`migrate-create` (the standalone golang-migrate CLI, for
# manual/CI use outside the running binary) read DATABASE_MIGRATION_URL
# instead — a separate variable, same default value.
MIGRATION_DATABASE_URL=postgres://tender_acl:tender_acl@localhost:5536/tender_acl?sslmode=disable
DATABASE_MIGRATION_URL=postgres://tender_acl:tender_acl@localhost:5536/tender_acl?sslmode=disable

# Pool sizing — pgcommon.ConfigFromEnv() (defaults shown; safe to omit).
# PG_BOUNCER_MODE is deliberately NOT here: cmd/tender-acl/main.go forces
# PGBouncerMode=true unconditionally regardless of this var (transaction-
# scoped RLS GUCs are required no matter the topology, not a tunable).
PG_MAX_CONNS=10
PG_MIN_CONNS=2
PG_SLOW_QUERY_THRESHOLD=200ms

# ── Valkey / Redis ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The only cache region: tac:acl:{tenant}:{tender}:{user}, fixed 30s TTL
# (LLD §9, hardcoded — not independently configurable via env var).
VALKEY_ADDR=localhost:6382
VALKEY_PASSWORD=

# ── Membership check (LLD §6.3, §7.6.2) ─────────────────────────────────
# The one synchronous outbound dependency: a grant-time-only, fail-closed
# check against iam-org-membership's internal provider endpoint
# (GET /api/v1/internal/tenants/:id/members/:user_id/exists — see
# O_AND_M_DELTA.md; this is a stable, working contract).
# Point this at a locally running iam-org-membership instance for full
# local TAC-2 testing. ≤50ms p99 expected latency; 300ms hard client
# timeout — these are deliberately different numbers, do not conflate them.
CORE_INTERNAL_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080
MEMBERSHIP_CHECK_TIMEOUT_MS=300

# ── AWS SQS (TenantOffboarded consumer — receive-only, publishes nothing) ─
# Points at the LocalStack container from docker-compose.yml (`make
# docker-up` / `make compose-up`), which scripts/init-localstack.sh
# provisions with tenant-lifecycle-tenderacl-q + its DLQ on startup. The
# host-side port is 4569 (4566/4567/4568 are claimed by sibling services
# running alongside this one — iam-user-profile2 / iam-org-membership /
# iam-group-mapping). Production overrides all four of these with the real
# queue URLs/region and drops the static credentials entirely in favor of
# IRSA (see deploy/iam/).
SQS_QUEUE_URL=http://localhost:4569/000000000000/tenant-lifecycle-tenderacl-q
SQS_DLQ_URL=http://localhost:4569/000000000000/tenant-lifecycle-tenderacl-q-dlq
# SQS_QUEUE_URL and this one are loaded by platform-events/pkg/config.LoadSQS
# (not this service's own config.go) — 4, not LoadSQS's own default of 1, to
# match this queue's previous CONSUMER_CONCURRENCY-driven behavior. Other
# LoadSQS tunables (SQS_MAX_MESSAGES/SQS_WAIT_SECONDS/
# SQS_VISIBILITY_TIMEOUT/SQS_MAX_RECEIVE_COUNT) are left unset — library
# defaults (10/20s/30s/unset) apply.
SQS_CONCURRENCY=4
# ADR-0007 Wave 3 Phase 3 (O_AND_M_DELTA.md §5 Option B) — the per-user-
# removal ACL cascade, a second/independent subscription. This queue has no
# platform-events/pkg/config equivalent (LoadSQS only covers one queue per
# service), so it stays hand-rolled via CONSUMER_CONCURRENCY below.
MEMBER_REMOVAL_SQS_QUEUE_URL=http://localhost:4569/000000000000/member-removal-tenderacl-q
MEMBER_REMOVAL_SQS_DLQ_URL=http://localhost:4569/000000000000/member-removal-tenderacl-q-dlq
AWS_REGION=us-east-1
AWS_ENDPOINT_URL=http://localhost:4569
# Dummy static credentials — required so aws-sdk-go-v2's credential chain
# resolves from these env vars instead of falling through to the EC2 IMDS
# provider, which fails outside EC2 with "no EC2 IMDS role found ... host
# is down".
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=localstack
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=localstack
# member-removal-tenderacl-q's concurrency only — see SQS_CONCURRENCY above
# for tenant-lifecycle-tenderacl-q's.
CONSUMER_CONCURRENCY=4

# ── Observability ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# gRPC, not HTTP — tracing now goes through platform-gincommon's
# ObservabilityMiddlewares (OTLP/gRPC, default port 4317), not a hand-rolled
# otlptracehttp exporter. Bare host:port, no scheme — do not prefix with
# http://.
OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=localhost:4317

# Docs surface: /swagger (generated OpenAPI spec, `make swag`), /asyncapi +
# /asyncapi.yaml (rendered HTML catalog + raw spec for api/asyncapi.yaml,
# compiled into the binary via api/embed.go — not read from disk), /healthz,
# /readyz. Swagger/AsyncAPI routes are always mounted outside production;
# DOCS_ENABLED opts both into production too, and DOCS_AUTH_TOKEN (if set)
# additionally bearer-auth-gates them there.
DOCS_ENABLED=false
DOCS_AUTH_TOKEN=
